I think they don't try to obtain "that AC." Serial ascenders (and I count
myself in this number these days, though there are still many players
better than I am) are more practiced and comfortable with tactics and
strategy at lower armor class, and thus taking a higher-risk approach
like the protection racket is unnecessary, thus there's no point to doing
it. I have no doubt that the racket is often successful in the hands
of an experienced racketeer --- in fact, in my string of 6 ascensions
(my longest), two of them were games where I got to minetown at XL 3 or
4 --- but to a lot of players, the question is "Why bother?" AC -15 at
DL10 just isn't useful to some of us, and jumping through hoops to get
there is counterproductive.

