So if you look at marvin or sawtooth or someone like that, you'll see
that class doesn't seem to matter for them, but not all of us are quite
that strong. My string of six was as follows:

 1. Wiz-Elf-Fem-Cha, who had a wand of wishing early on so it was easy
 2. Ran-Hum-Mal-Neu, who killed things from afar
 3. Val-Dwa-Fem-Law, who was a tank, and actually a protection run (I found
    a magic whistle and hit Minetown at XL4, I wasn't really trying for it
    but since I was there, and the Priest was there, why not?)
 4. Rog-Orc-Fem-Cha, because Elbereth is just so powerful; armor didn't
    matter because nothing could touch me.
 5. Arc-Gno-Mal-Neu, who also hit Minetown at XL4 or so, and did benefit
    more from this, because my missile weapon options were for crap
 6. Sam-Hum-Fem-Law, who I played with yumi and ya through the first half
    of the game, actually.

The characters who are most worth protection running, in my opinion, are
those who need to be able to soak melee damage because they are too lame 
to use good ranged attacks early in the game:

 * Archaeologist
 * Barbarian
 * Caveman (slings do not count as good)
 * Knight? ... probably
 * Monk maybe, if you don't start with the Sleep spell
 * Priest

For these characters, AC is more of a benefit, because they are more
likely to run into situations where they have to be next to something
to kill it.  Monks especially need to get close to things to kill them
until they find a good enough set of spells, and they can't wear body
armor to boot. When I play monks, I make a point of throwing daggers or
darts anyway, just to minimize the melee damage I take. I also do this
with priests. The others do enough melee damage that I don't find it
very important.

And of course there are those classes who, though they can get to Skilled
or Expert with a respectable ranged weapon, start the game reasonably
tricked out to do the racket such that it might be worthwhile:

 * Healer
 * Tourist

My one healer ascension was a racket, and so was my healer-choked-on-a-
wraith-corpse-at-XL-30 (*shame*), but I've always felt that tourists don't
have enough outs to be mucking around with that, and want the HP more.
But I don't have a lot of experience with tourists, I ascended one and
moved on. Someone else may be able to comment more usefully.

Fundamentally, I think that the problem protection running tries to solve
is "I'm taking too much damage from melee attacks." It solves the symptom
by reducing the damage, but rather than a pound of cure, how about an
ounce of prevention: Stop meleeing things! Pay more attention! If you're
getting killed by mumakil, you are doing it wrong. They're speed nine
and respect Elbereth. If you're getting killed by swarms of monsters,
use hallways better, use ranged weapons, and use Elbereth.

Even without Elbereth, you can still avoid taking lots of melee damage
with smart play; no one would suggest that illiterates need to do the
protection racket to be viable. (Neither of mine did.)

But honestly? "Pick what makes you ascend, and do that."

